# YourPHR — Docker / docker-compose bootstrap
#
#   cp .env.docker.example .env
#
# NOTHING here is required by the application. The image's shipped defaults are already correct
# for a container, so a stock `docker compose up` works with an empty file.
# Everything else is changed at Admin -> Configuration. See docs/configuration-system.md.

# --- read by docker-compose.yml, NOT by the app ---
# These substitute ${...} inside the compose file to decide what gets published on the host.
HOSTNAME=fasten
IP=0.0.0.0
PORT=9090
domainname=example.com

# --- optional application settings ---

# At-rest database encryption is ON by default. The first-run setup wizard prompts for a key, so
# you do not have to set one here — but supplying it in advance skips that step and lets an
# unattended deploy come up on its own.
#   generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# NOTE: while encryption is on, backup and restore are refused (see docs/deployment/README.md).
# To run unencrypted instead, set YOURPHR_DATABASE_ENCRYPTION_ENABLED=false.
# YOURPHR_DATABASE_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Label stamped into backup filenames, to tell instances apart in a shared folder.
# YOURPHR_BACKUP_LABEL=

# The compose files start a C-CDA converter sidecar and the app is pointed at it by default.
# Set this to false if you removed the sidecar; XML import then fails with a clear error.
# YOURPHR_CDA_CONVERTER_ENABLED=true

# --- Chat (yourphr#594): ask questions about your own records ---
#
# OFF by default. Needs a language-model endpoint YOU run — nothing here reaches a hosted model.
# Full setup, including the two providers: docs/deployment/chat.md
#
# 'local' is the native provider: it searches your records where they already are, so there is no
# extra container, no second copy of your records, and nothing to index or backfill. Transcripts go
# in the app database, encrypted with everything else.
#
# YOURPHR_CHAT_PROVIDER=local
#   any OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint. Ollama: http://<host>:11434 (no /v1 suffix).
#   Load the model first — `ollama run <name>` — pulling alone is not enough.
# YOURPHR_CHAT_MODEL_URL=
#   the model as your endpoint names it. No prefix.
# YOURPHR_CHAT_MODEL_NAME=medgemma:27b-it-q4_K_M
#   How many records one answer may draw on. More is NOT better on a small model: measured on a 4B,
#   20 records made it refuse and 30 made it list lab tests as diagnoses. A 27B improved up to 25.
# YOURPHR_CHAT_RETRIEVAL_MAX_RECORDS=10
#   Bytes of record text one answer may carry.
# YOURPHR_CHAT_MODEL_MAX_BYTES=57344
#
# The ported alternative, which keeps a second copy of every record in the Typesense sidecar in
# docker-compose.yml. Only for instances already running it — see the comparison in the doc.
# YOURPHR_CHAT_PROVIDER=typesense
#   also becomes the sidecar's TYPESENSE_API_KEY — generate with: openssl rand -hex 16
# YOURPHR_CHAT_TYPESENSE_API_KEY=
